_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gabegorelick/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gabegorelick/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gabegorelick/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gabegorelick/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gabegorelick/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gabegorelick/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gabegorelick/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"@manast That would actually cause the user's error to *not* be returned in the following case:\r\n```js\r\nqueue.process(function(job, callback) {\r\n  jobDone(new Error());\r\n});\r\n```\r\n\r\nInstead, a `Bluebird.OperationalError` would be passed to the `failed` handler. This arguably leaks implementation details to the caller and would be a change in API since it's not currently returned. It would also break this test case that explicitly checks for this:\r\nhttps://github.com/OptimalBits/bull/blob/cf2c6883fc2d861397bd59df7186b730800655e0/test/test_queue.js#L1208-L1232\r\n\r\nMy PR was an attempt to have the best of both worlds: unwrap Bull's internal error but don't unwrap too much.","created_at":"2018-10-08T15:43:16Z","updated_at":"2018-10-08T15:52:29Z","html_url":"https://github.com/OptimalBits/bull/pull/1079#discussion_r223411488","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OptimalBits/bull/pulls/1079","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/OptimalBits/bull/pulls/comments/223411488"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/OptimalBits/bull/pull/1079#discussion_r223411488"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/OptimalBits/bull/pulls/1079"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OptimalBits/bull/pulls/comments/223411488/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line